msgid "ad.tip.toggle"
msgstr "A toggle switches its targets on or off from the menu. Drag an object onto the tree, or add an effect below, to give it something to switch."

msgid "ad.tip.radial"
msgstr "A radial blends its targets between two ends as its slider moves, instead of switching them on or off. Add a blend shape below and set what its low and high ends look like."

msgid "ad.tip.submenu"
msgstr "A submenu groups other entries under one menu button. Drag entries into it, or add new ones while it is selected, to fill it."

msgid "ad.tip.trigger"
msgstr "A trigger fires its effects on its own, from a toggle, a parameter, a touch or a blend shape, without taking a menu slot of its own. Pick what starts it below."

msgid "ad.tip.override"
msgstr "An override holds a blend shape at one value in every animation that already uses it, so nothing else can fight it. Add the shape it should hold below."

msgid "ad.tip.preset"
msgstr "A preset puts several other controls into one state with a single button. Add the states it should set below."

msgid "ad.tip.grabbable"
msgstr "A grabbable lets a creator pick up and hold an object in a hand. Pick the object and which hand or hands below."

msgid "ad.tip.animator"
msgstr "A merged animator brings an existing controller's layers straight into the build, unchanged. Pick the controller below."

msgid "ad.tip.menu_asset"
msgstr "An installed menu asset brings a finished menu asset into the build as it already is. Pick the asset above."

msgid "ad.tip.header"
msgstr "This header holds the component's own install settings and the avatar's shared memory bar. Add your first entry in the tree below to get started."

msgid "ad.tip.header.simple"
msgstr "This header shows whether the avatar is ready to upload and how much of VRChat's memory the menu uses. Add your first entry in the tree below to get started."

msgid "ad.ui.mode.simple"
msgstr "Simple"

msgid "ad.ui.mode.advanced"
msgstr "Advanced"

msgid "ad.ui.mode.tip"
msgstr "Simple shows only what most avatars need; Advanced shows every tool. Nothing you made is hidden."

msgid "ad.ui.advanced_item.note"
msgstr "This is an advanced item; switch to Advanced to add more like it."

msgid "ad.warn.link_clips_outside_fx"
msgstr "\"{0}\" follows {1}, but that shape also moves in {2}, outside the FX layer, where the trigger cannot see it. Move that animation into the FX layer if the trigger should react to it there."

msgid "ad.warn.link_source_tracked"
msgstr "\"{0}\" follows {1}, which VRChat moves itself for blinking or lip sync outside every animation, so the trigger never sees it move. Pick a shape your own animations move instead. ({2})"

msgid "ad.warn.smooth_range"
msgstr "\"{0}\" starts at {1} but is fully on at {2}, which is not above it, so it is fully on just above Starts at instead. Set Fully on at higher than Starts at. ({3})"

msgid "ad.warn.requirements_one_card"
msgstr "\"{0}\" reads only the card its shape is in, so the conditions in its other cards are kept but not used. Move what you need into the first card with + And, or remove the other cards. ({1})"

